{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAQTmgNephBZzSHmqdoy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `Hijack` in `response_writer.go` so it only refuses once body data has been written. Before, it also refused after the headers alone had been sent (for example via `WriteHeaderNow` or `Flush`). Some websocket libraries send the upgrade response headers and then hijack the connection, so that check broke them. Hijacking after body data is written still returns `errHijackAlreadyWritten`.\n\nI added a test case that sends headers and then hijacks, which must succeed. The gate passed: the Hijack tests fail without the fix and pass with it. I only ran those tests, not the full suite, and I haven't tried it with a real websocket library."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1361,"cache_read_input_tokens":33133,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1361,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":212,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ba367f3-f5b0-45ff-8105-43ef21c206da","uuid":"da4a5cb5-eca8-4828-b80a-456e8e825a05","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:22:56.948Z","request_id":"req_011CgAQTmUieAsApNeV39KTY"}
